# Service endpoints, in the open on purpose.
#
# THIS FILE IS COMMITTED. Nothing secret goes in it — these are the public hosts a
# build talks to, and having them here rather than as literals in three source files
# means changing one is a one-line diff a non-author can review, not a hunt through
# packages/ for whichever constant happens to be the one that is read.
#
# Secrets go in .env.local, which .gitignore excludes.
#
# Two names for the same value because two bundlers are involved and neither reads
# the other's:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_*  Metro inlines it into the mobile bundle at build time. Only this
#                  prefix is inlined — a differently-named variable silently becomes
#                  `undefined` on device, with the fallback quietly taking over.
#   NEXUS_*        Read by the desktop build (apps/desktop/build-main.mjs) and baked
#                  into the Electron main bundle, so a packaged app does not depend
#                  on whatever environment the user happens to launch it from.
#
# tools/check-env.mjs fails if the two ever disagree.

# MessageBox — where handle payments are delivered and collected.
EXPO_PUBLIC_MESSAGEBOX_URL=https://gmb.bsvblockchain.tech
NEXUS_MESSAGEBOX_URL=https://gmb.bsvblockchain.tech
